

  Introduction
  ------------

   This chapter contains a short description of all programs (Executables)
   contained in the Trion BBS distribution archive.

   A full description of all programs can be found in the
   "Trion:docs/utils/" directory where a document for each program
   can be found.

   Doors usually have a document in the directory where they
   are stored. These can be found a subdirectory of the 
   "Doors:" or "Trion:doors/" directory.



  List of all programs
  --------------------

   general programs
   ----------------

   bbs                 <-  The BBS executable
   trionRM             <-  The (TRION) Resource Manager
   trion               <-  Gives commands to the BBS nodes
   caller              <-  Util to call other systems several times
   CheckStart          <-  Asks if the BBS system should be started
   ClickitX            <-  GuiTools obsolete with GuiMod
   convertusers        <-  tool used to upgrade to new versions
   Event               <-  tool to stop the Trion scheduler
   filecmp             <-  tool to compare files
   freq                <-  To freq files or search for a phone number
   GuiMod              <-  Gui tool to operate the system
   menu                <-  The Menu Compiler
   MaintMod            <-  Maintenance monitor
   bbstext             <-  Compiles bbstext configuration files
   listnodes           <-  Gives a list with the actions of the BBS nodes
   RMCommander         <-  Gives commandos to the Resource Manager
   Scheduler           <-  Cron like util to start programms
   TopDL               <-  Makes a screen with the top Up/down loaders
   TTrimLogs           <-  Shrinks the logs to a configured size
   Unpack              <-  Front end for archivers
   UserEd              <-  The trion offline GUI User editor
   WaitNodes           <-  Waits until there are no users logged in
   TrionHotKeys        <-  Installs a commodity to hotkey nodes.
   SetCalls            <-  Set the total number of calls
   SyncClock           <-  Synchronize the clock with an other machine
   AddSysop            <-  Define a sysop (for configuring purposes)

   File related programs
   ---------------------

   CheckFileBase       <-  Util to operate on the filebase
   FileEd              <-  The Trion offline GUI file editor
   TBulkUpload         <-  Adds files in the File dirs wich are not already in the calatog
   TAF                 <-  Trion AllFiles .. makes and adds an allfiles list

   mail related programs
   ---------------------

   AreaFix             <-  Trion AreaFix programm
   CheckIfMail         <-  Checks if there is mail for a BBS node
   CheckInbound        <-  Checks if there is anything in the Inbound
   KillOldMail         <-  this removes mail from the outbound after x days
   maildecode          <-  programm to decode UUencoded and Base64 coded files
   PointScan           <-  Makes a list of all the mailers used
   Poll                <-  Makes a 'poll packet' to call a system
   TMP                 <-  The (TRION) Mail Processor
   TrionTick           <-  A tick util to process tick files
   ViewPacket          <-  tool to check mail packets

   doors
   -----

   Conf                <-  Conference system between nodes
   Demodoor            <-  Version of the Trion Demo Clidoor
   SendNodeMsg         <-  System to send messages to other nodes
   FreeSpace           <-  Shows the amount of freespace on your upload HD
   TrionTetris         <-  Tetris door game
   Quest               <-  Doors for the questionair system
   ChatDoor            <-  Split screen chat door
                           Line chat doot with log
                           A 'page sysop' door wich asks for a chat reason
                           RoboChat doors
   fsed                <-  Full screen editor for mail
   FX                  <-  Doors to add effects to ANSI menus
   lastcallers         <-  Lastcallers and UsageGraph doors
   TrionCDdoor         <-  Door to access CDrom drives
   TrionLOP            <-  Trion Log off police
   TrionText           <-  Teletext emulation door
   altscr              <-  Tool to rotate screens
   NlToScr             <-  Makes a screen from nodelists



